text:
AI is moving past the chatbot stage.

The stack is splitting into models, payments, connectors, and safety.

@corentAI is making the model side simpler: one key, access to different models, a spend ceiling, and support across image, video, voice, and text.

@Ripple is working on machine payments through the XRP Ledger, giving agents a way to pay for data and compute.

@Templafy is using MCP to turn AI output into finished, branded presentations.

@GoPlusSecurity is giving agents tools to investigate security issues instead of just making guesses.

And @GoogleDeepMind keeps pushing AI further across voice, research, and weather.

It’s not just about which model gives the best answer anymore.

Give an agent a job, the right tools, and clear limits, and let it do the work.

That’s the layer that matters.
